The revisionist is aggrieved with the impugned order and has assailed the same on various grounds which can be summarized as under:-
(i) That the Ld. Trial Court passed the impugned order in mechanical manner with finding contrary to the fact and ordered to frame the charge without having prima facie case against the revisionist;
(ii) That the Ld. Trial Court framed the charges even though Crl Rev No. 35/2025 Neetu Gupta vs. State & Ors.

Page No. 3 of 15 essential ingredients of the offences are Neetu Gupta vs Govt Of Nct Of Delhi And Ors on 4 September, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/19800725/
2 not made out on the basis of the material placed on record;
(iii) That the Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate that the allegations in the complaint are general and vague in nature and made to harass the revisionist;
(iv) That the Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate that in the FIR there were no specific allegations qua revisionist and the complainant made the supplementary statement in order to make the allegation;
(v) That the Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate that this FIR is registered as a matrimonial dispute and the complainant made the general allegations against all the family members of her husband;
(vi) That the Ld. Trial Court failed to appreciate that the revisionist/accused was married and residing with her family and at the time of alleged incident she was suffering from Covid virus and was admitted in the hospital on 21.04.2021 and her father-in-law had expired on 22.04.2021.
